  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**The configuration is correct, but nothing links it to the requirement.**\n\n**Configuration.** `book.toml` lines 11–16, in `[output.html]`, set exactly what the requirement asks for:\n- `git-repository-url = \"https://github.com/nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem\"`\n- `edit-url-template = \"https://github.com/nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem/edit/main/{path}\"`\n\nThe first covers the repository link for `nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem`. The second sets page edit links to the `main` branch.\n\n**References.** `references` for `requirements.layout.repository_links` returns no sites. No `{impl}`, `{test}` or `{cite}` marker points at it.\n- The `[output.html]` table in `book.toml` carries no `{impl}` annotation. `book.toml` does annotate other tables, for example `{impl}` on `requirements.cli.mdbook` at the end of the `[book]` table, so the convention is available.\n- The unmarked configuration is the implementation of this requirement. Under the assessment rules, code that implements a requirement without an `{impl}` reference is a gap.\n\n**Tests.** Nothing checks that `book.toml` has these two settings.\n- The test `source_links_use_configured_repository_and_branch` in `src/index.rs` is cited only for `requirements.index.source_links`. It uses synthetic configs for `example/project`, not this project's `book.toml`.\n- A small test could parse `book.toml` and assert both values. That is easy, so the absence of any test is not justified by simplicity or impracticality.\n\n**Acknowledged gaps.** I found no FIXME comments for these gaps. The determination is therefore false, not FIXME.",
